[Event "London vs ...d5"]

{White builds a pyramid of pawns on c3, d4 and e3, with the bishop on f4 outside the chain. Plans include Ne5 and f4, or a kingside attack with Bd3, Qf3 and h4.}
1. d4 {Takes the centre.}
1... d5 {Black matches.}
2. Bf4 {[%cal Gf4b8] The London: the bishop develops before e3 locks it in.}
2... Nf6 {Development.}
(2... c5 {Black strikes at d4.}
 3. e3 {Solid.}
 3... Nc6 {Pressure on d4.}
 4. c3 {[%csl Gd4] Holds d4.}
 4... Qb6 {[%cal Gb6b2] Hits b2, the classic London weakness.}
 5. Qb3 {Offers a queen trade, which would double Black's pawns.}
 5... c4 {Gains queenside space.}
 6. Qc2 {Retreats.}
 6... Bf5 {Challenges the queen.}
 7. Qc1 {[%csl Gb2] Defends b2.})
(2... Bf5 {Black mirrors.}
 3. e3 {Solid.}
 3... e6 {Solid.}
 4. Nd2 {Supports Ngf3 and keeps the c-pawn flexible.}
 4... Nf6 {Development.}
 5. Ngf3 {Development.}
 5... Bd6 {[%cal Gd6f4] Challenges the f4-bishop.}
 6. Bg3 {Avoids the exchange.}
 6... O-O {Castles.}
 7. Be2 {Solid.})
3. e3 {Solid.}
3... e6 {Solid.}
(3... c5 {Strikes at d4.}
 4. c3 {Holds d4.}
 4... Nc6 {Pressure.}
 5. Nd2 {Development.}
 5... Qb6 {Hits b2.}
 6. Qb3 {Offers the trade.}
 6... c4 {Space.}
 7. Qc2 {Retreats.}
 7... Bf5 {Tempo on the queen.}
 8. Qc1 {Defends.})
4. Nf3 {Development.}
4... c5 {Strikes at d4.}
5. c3 {Holds d4.}
5... Nc6 {Development.}
6. Nbd2 {[%cal Gd2e4] Supports e4 and f3.}
6... Bd6 {Challenges the f4-bishop.}
7. Bg3 {[%csl Gh2] Keeps the bishop. If ...Bxg3, hxg3 opens the h-file.}
7... O-O {Castles.}
8. Bd3 {[%cal Gd3h7] Aims at h7.}
8... b6 {Prepares ...Bb7.}
9. Ne5 {[%csl Ge5] The London outpost.}
9... Bb7 {Development.}
10. f4 {[%cal Gf4f5] Supports e5 and prepares a kingside attack.} *

[Event "London vs ...Nf6/...g6"]

{Against King's Indian setups, White keeps the structure solid and plays h3, Be2 and O-O, sometimes with a4 or c4.}
1. d4 {Takes the centre.}
1... Nf6 {Development.}
2. Bf4 {The London.}
2... g6 {A King's Indian setup.}
(2... e6 {Solid.}
 3. e3 {Solid.}
 3... c5 {Strikes at d4.}
 4. c3 {Holds d4.}
 4... Nc6 {Development.}
 5. Nd2 {Development.}
 5... d5 {The centre.}
 6. Ngf3 {Development.}
 6... Bd6 {Challenges the bishop.}
 7. Bg3 {Keeps it.}
 7... O-O {Castles.}
 8. Bd3 {[%cal Gd3h7] Aims at h7.})
(2... d6 {Prepares ...e5.}
 3. e3 {Solid.}
 3... g6 {Fianchetto.}
 4. Nc3 {Watches e4.}
 4... Bg7 {Development.}
 5. Nf3 {Development.}
 5... O-O {Castles.}
 6. Be2 {Development.}
 6... c5 {Strikes at d4.}
 7. O-O {King safety.})
